---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import data from "../data/controlbun.json";

// A styled 404, because the default one threw the site away.
//
// Astro's built-in is a dark monospace framework page with no header, no
// navigation and no way home, against a light serif site. A stranger reading the
// site cold hit it twice: once on a nonsense URL, and once by trimming
// /<owner>/<model>/<label>/<version>/ back to reach the label view, which is the
// guess a GitHub-shaped URL trains you to make. Being lost is the one moment the
// header matters most and it was the one moment it disappeared.
//
// The trimming case is worth answering rather than just surviving, so the shapes
// are listed. They are the routes `[...path].astro` actually builds, and a reader
// who guessed wrong can see which segment they dropped.
//
// `synthetic="none"` because this page publishes no figure at all, so the
// corpus marker would be describing nothing.

const models = data.model_index.map((m) => m.model_id).sort();
---

<Base title="Not found" trail={[{ text: "controlbun", href: "/" }]} synthetic="none">
  <h1 slot="heading">Not found</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    There is nothing at this address. That is a fact about the URL rather than
    about the registry: nothing here has been moved or withdrawn.
  </p>

  <h2>The shapes that exist</h2>

  <dl class="spec">
    <dt class="mono">/models/</dt>
    <dd>Every model anything has been published against.</dd>

    <dt class="mono">/models/&lt;model&gt;/</dt>
    <dd>Our index entry for one model. The model itself lives elsewhere.</dd>

    <dt class="mono">/models/&lt;model&gt;/&lt;label&gt;/</dt>
    <dd>Everyone claiming that label against that model, side by side.</dd>

    <dt class="mono">/&lt;owner&gt;/&lt;model&gt;/&lt;label&gt;/&lt;version&gt;/</dt>
    <dd>
      One submission. The version is part of the address because
      <span class="mono">author/label@version</span> is the identity here and
      nothing above it resolves to a single artifact.
    </dd>

    <dt class="mono">/owners/</dt>
    <dd>Everyone who has taken part, whether or not they published an artifact.</dd>

    <dt class="mono">/&lt;owner&gt;/</dt>
    <dd>One person, and what they actually did.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="note">
    A label has no page of its own. Claimants of the same word on different models
    are not comparable, so there is nowhere sensible to put them together.
  </p>

  <h2>Models in the registry</h2>

  <ul class="plain">
    {models.map((id) => (
      <li><a class="mono" href={`/models/${id}/`}>{id}</a></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p><a href="/">Back to the registry</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .plain { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .plain li { padding: .15rem 0; }
</style>
